From 0e7b09df7761334248a54e4d470f267c35fa9e6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:26:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] WebXR: offer the flat stereo display where an output
 shows stereo 3D

The flat stereo display (dom.vr.flat.enabled) is the screen as a WebXR
immersive device. It is now offered whenever an output shows stereo 3D,
or can: KWin lists a 3D mode for it (a display's own HDMI 1.4 3D modes,
or the virtual 3D modes its stereo toggles turn on, anaglyph and the
other formats), or pairs it with another output. The browser reads that
from kde_output_device_v2 (through kde_output_device_registry_v2, or the
per-output globals of older KWin) and keeps gfxVars::StereoOutputs
current as outputs come and go.

The person's main monitor can stay 2D: the page hands full side by
side, declared, as always, and KWin shows each output what it can, both
eyes on a 3D output and the left eye on a 2D one. The browser does
nothing per monitor.

Where no output does, the device is not offered, so pages take their
own 2D path: isSessionSupported("immersive-vr") resolves false,
requestSession() rejects with NotSupportedError, inline-stereo is not
granted, and the VR service does not start the flat session.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
